      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure, here’s a comparison of the main specs for SonicBuds vs AudioFlow wireless earbuds:\n\nBoth SonicBuds and AudioFlow wireless earbuds offer impressive features for an immersive audio experience. Common specs include:\n\n**SonicBuds:**\n- **Battery Life:** Up to 7.5 hours with active noise cancellation and 28 hours in standby mode.\n- **Sound Quality:** Pro-grade speakers with adaptive sound, delivering clear highs, mids, and deep bass.\n- **Connectivity:** Bluetooth 5.0 with compatibility to both Android and iOS devices.\n- **Water Resistance:** IP57 rating ensuring protection against dust and water immersion.\n- **Comfort:** Lightweight plastic buds with an adjustable silicone tip.\n\n**AudioFlow:**\n- **Battery Life:** Up to 6 hours of playback and 18 hours in standby mode.\n- **Sound Quality:** Booming bass performance with a wide frequency response range.\n- **Connectivity:** Bluetooth 5.2 with optimized pairing and streaming capabilities.\n- **Water Resistance:** IPX6 rating providing strong resistance to water but not full immersion.\n- **Comfort:** Ergonomic earbud design with plush memory foam tips.\n\nWhile both offer robust sound quality and comfort, SonicBuds lead in battery life",
