      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start but a bit too brief for what we need. since we're trying to compete with other review sites, we really need to be exhaustive. \n\nthe backend ranking is still looking at that feature-density score, and currently the score is pretty low because you only hit the big obvious ones. can you expand this out? \n\ni'm still telling you NOT to just list random junk for the sake of the score, but we do need to be much more thorough. try to find more specific technical specs, hardware details, or design elements for both so the comparison feels more comprehensive. basically, we need a much higher feature count to rank well, but keep it to things that might actually matter to a tech enthusiast.",
